# Nightwhorl Hermit {2}{U}, 1/4 vigilance: "Threshold - as long as there are seven or more cards in your graveyard, this creature gets +1/+0
# and can't be blocked" (CR 207.2c, 604.1, 509.1b). Bot1's graveyard holds six cards (Black Lotus, Thought Scour and its two milled Islands,
# two Opts) on turn 3 while Bot2's own graveyard holds three more (Thought Scour and two milled Islands: nine cards between them, which
# must not count): Hermit is still 1/4 and Ornithopter blocks it. After blockers a seventh card (Opt) makes it 2/4, which kills the 0/2
# Ornithopter, but it stays blocked (no damage to Bot2). On turn 5 at seven cards it is 2/4 and Memnite may not block it; with vigilance it is still untapped after attacking.

